# Stripe TEST-mode sandbox checkout (GOL-688 / GOL-696 / GOL-899). grove_headless
# reads these as LOWERCASE env (controllers/main.py) — this is the ONLY key the
# checkout SESSION route (/grove/api/v1/checkout/session) reads. All three
# storefronts proxy to it (thin-proxy PRs #278/#279, GOL-890), so an empty value
# here 503s "Checkout is not configured yet" for ggg + goldberry + nursery alike.
# The apply-time `op` account MUST be grove-devops-ro (reads Grove QA + Admin);
# the Admin-only SA resolves Grove QA refs to "" and silently disables checkout.
#   secret_key    → Grove QA vault, item stripe-nursery-qa, field secret_key (below).
#   webhook_secret → whsec_ from the Terra-registered QA endpoint (we_1Tw4NO...),
#     stored on Admin/Grove Infra (grove-qa is read-only to us; can't write it back).
#
# DECISION 2026-07-30 (Josh, GOL-899): use the existing `stripe-nursery-qa` Grove
# QA item as the shared backend key. A prior run commented this out intending to
# mint a dedicated `stripe-odoo-backend-qa` item (scope purity + avoid coupling),
# but that left NO backend key provisioned and silently 503'd checkout for all
# three storefronts once the thin proxies made this env the only path. Josh's
# call: the nursery restricted rk_test_ key is the QA test secret key; its scope
# is empirically sufficient (it creates live Checkout Sessions — GOL-956). Same
# item/field as TF_VAR_stripe_secret_key_nursery above.
#   PROD TODO (do NOT carry this coupling to production): prod must use a
#   DEDICATED backend key, not a storefront key — revoking either must not break
#   the other. Tracked in docs/RUNBOOK-checkout-stripe-guardrails.md.
TF_VAR_stripe_test_secret_key="op://Grove QA/gi4l6bmv45tyc2uwphutkrd2um/qkd4ehby6hy4np6ymxkssngqqu"
TF_VAR_stripe_test_webhook_secret="op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/qvkpvg24x2wbsn6owjyvn4vhx4/tkgu5xgoc4iidhb42dd6k6ue4m"
